WEBVTT

00:08.541 --> 00:13.501
Kashima Mountain
Mountain Trail

00:20.653 --> 00:21.847
Tomari...

00:22.889 --> 00:25.449
She was always by my side...

00:25.759 --> 00:28.023
<i>Ever since I was little...</i>

00:28.128 --> 00:29.595
Always...

00:32.665 --> 00:36.066
She's the girl who
understands me best.

00:37.470 --> 00:40.439
I like you a lot, Tomari.

00:48.415 --> 00:49.347
Yasuna...

00:50.650 --> 00:55.314
She seems lonely, but provides
me with the power to live...

00:56.589 --> 00:59.353
...a girl who plays
the flute wonderfully.

01:02.862 --> 01:04.727
My first love.

01:05.799 --> 01:06.959
Yasuna...

01:07.834 --> 01:09.699
I really like you.

01:21.214 --> 01:22.181
I..

01:22.749 --> 01:27.118
<i>Maybe I didn't take it
seriously since we're all girls...</i>

01:28.321 --> 01:30.755
<i>...and I ended up hurting them.</i>

01:32.125 --> 01:34.923
To really like someone...

01:35.395 --> 01:36.794
What is...

01:38.098 --> 01:39.497
...love?

01:42.735 --> 01:48.071
Kashimashi
~Girl Meets Girl~

02:28.081 --> 02:31.050
Summer is about to end soon...

02:31.518 --> 02:36.683
Love Begins at Last

02:36.990 --> 02:39.185
What? She went out?

02:39.292 --> 02:40.384
I see...

02:42.362 --> 02:44.330
Thank you very much.

03:08.221 --> 03:09.279
Tomari!

03:09.389 --> 03:11.084
Hey, you're here.

03:11.958 --> 03:13.619
What's wrong?

03:13.960 --> 03:19.227
Well, I stopped by your house
and was told you went out, so...

03:19.699 --> 03:23.658
<i>You came to my house?
I guess we missed each other then...</i>

03:24.337 --> 03:28.296
<i>You weren't home,
so I figured you'd come here.</i>

03:28.841 --> 03:30.934
<i>I wanted to talk to you...</i>

03:31.044 --> 03:32.102
Talk?

03:32.212 --> 03:34.578
Well, it's really nothing...

03:34.948 --> 03:35.548
Tomari...

03:35.548 --> 03:36.913
Tomari...
Well...

03:37.016 --> 03:39.484
I need to talk to you too.

03:40.119 --> 03:41.950
<i>Can I talk to you?</i>

03:43.623 --> 03:44.612
Sure.

03:44.724 --> 03:48.182
Well, you see... It's like this...

03:48.294 --> 03:49.352
What?

03:49.462 --> 03:51.259
Well, it's like...

03:51.531 --> 03:52.465
You know...

03:52.465 --> 03:53.432
You know...
I'll tell you!

03:53.433 --> 03:53.899
I'll tell you!

03:54.801 --> 03:58.897
1 told myself that I'd tell you
all about it, so I'll tell you.

03:59.038 --> 04:00.198
Hazumu...

04:01.608 --> 04:04.133
I've been thinking for a long time...

04:05.178 --> 04:09.114
<i>...about what I should do,
and what I want to do.</i>

04:10.216 --> 04:14.346
<i>I knew I had to decide.
I thought about it every day...</i>

04:14.554 --> 04:16.317
So ll decided.

04:17.123 --> 04:19.853
I'm going to stay by Yasuna's side.

04:29.269 --> 04:30.258
I see...

04:30.803 --> 04:32.031
<i>I'm sorry!</i>

04:32.138 --> 04:35.369
I'm glad I know how you feel. But...

04:36.576 --> 04:38.441
Sorry, my hand slipped.

04:38.544 --> 04:39.533
Tomari!

04:39.646 --> 04:42.046
I get it. Don't say any more.

04:42.148 --> 04:42.807
But...

04:42.915 --> 04:45.509
Wait! I'm seriously...

04:45.618 --> 04:47.586
I said I get it!

04:49.822 --> 04:53.588
<i>You probably know
what I want right now...</i>

04:55.561 --> 04:56.653
...don't you?

04:57.030 --> 04:58.231
What do you mean?

04:58.231 --> 04:59.498
<i>What do you mean?
This is what I mean!</i>

04:59.499 --> 05:00.158
<i>This is what I mean!</i>

05:01.034 --> 05:02.899
Stop it already!

05:03.002 --> 05:06.130
Take that!
Why don't you try to fight back...

05:07.740 --> 05:09.571
There's another hose!

05:10.643 --> 05:11.701
Hazumu...

05:12.845 --> 05:14.779
Hey, wait a minute!

05:14.881 --> 05:16.007
No way!

05:17.016 --> 05:18.108
Take that!

05:18.217 --> 05:19.684
Got you back!

05:19.786 --> 05:21.413
Take that and that!

05:21.521 --> 05:23.546
Take that and that and that!

05:23.656 --> 05:24.790
I'll get you 100 times more!

05:24.791 --> 05:26.782
I'll get you 100 times more!
Time out!

05:30.496 --> 05:33.056
Don't you think that was too much?

05:33.166 --> 05:35.225
You kept spraying me.

05:37.303 --> 05:39.203
Smells like the sun.

05:39.305 --> 05:40.203
Yeah.

05:40.873 --> 05:44.969
You liked wrapping yourself in
futons that were dried under the sun.

05:45.078 --> 05:48.206
We used to make futon piles
and hide under them...

05:48.314 --> 05:50.908
...and my mother would yell at us.

05:51.017 --> 05:55.181
She said the cotton would get
damaged, and she spanked you.

05:55.855 --> 05:59.621
I don't know why,
but she never spanked you.

05:59.726 --> 06:03.560
Because you're the one
who always started it.

06:03.730 --> 06:05.527
Your mother probably knew.

06:05.698 --> 06:08.667
But you enjoyed it too, right?

06:09.068 --> 06:14.131
Yeah... It felt warm and safe...
and it felt really good.

06:14.574 --> 06:17.771
I wanted to keep on
being like that forever.

06:21.547 --> 06:25.278
Hey, what did you want
to talk to me about?

06:25.485 --> 06:26.509
It's okay.

06:26.619 --> 06:27.608
Tell me.

06:28.788 --> 06:33.987
"1 want you to play with me one
last time. Then I'll give up on you."

06:35.528 --> 06:36.688
Tomari...

06:36.796 --> 06:39.321
<i>But you spoke before I did.</i>

06:40.466 --> 06:42.434
Well, I'm going home!

06:44.003 --> 06:45.971
Wait a minute, Tomari!

06:48.441 --> 06:50.841
Let's play for the entire day.

06:52.078 --> 06:53.306
Hazumu...

07:03.689 --> 07:13.690
Do you still remember
that childish promise?

07:15.768 --> 07:22.901
<i>You can't call them memories
since I was just being selfish.</i>

07:27.814 --> 07:34.185
<i>You haven't changed at all.
I'm happy every time I see you...</i>

07:34.287 --> 07:39.315
So let's just keep going...

07:39.826 --> 07:42.852
...forever.

07:43.596 --> 07:49.660
Time has passed, and all of
a sudden, we're becoming adults.

07:49.802 --> 07:55.900
I keep thinking that
1 want to be stronger.

07:56.042 --> 08:04.780
<i>But I want you to be
the person I knew just for today.</i>

08:05.184 --> 08:10.781
Let's create new memories.

08:21.033 --> 08:27.199
<i>Feelings that I have for you.
I can't even express...</i>

08:27.306 --> 08:33.302
<i>...half of what I feel,
but I'll be by your side.</i>

08:33.446 --> 08:39.316
But until this day ends...

08:39.519 --> 08:48.427
...I'm going to guide you to that sky.

08:54.700 --> 08:56.134
What did you wish for?

08:56.135 --> 08:58.160
What did you wish for?
Do you usually ask that?

08:58.271 --> 08:59.829
Why? Is it odd?

08:59.939 --> 09:02.203
I'll tell if you do.

09:02.275 --> 09:03.109
Me?

09:03.109 --> 09:05.737
Me?
See? Don't want to, right?

09:05.845 --> 09:08.143
It's not like that, but...

09:10.917 --> 09:13.909
I just wished for
Yasuna to get better...

09:14.787 --> 09:17.756
<i>Sorry, I shouldn't have told you that.</i>

09:20.393 --> 09:21.724
What about you?

09:21.827 --> 09:23.055
I'll pass.

09:23.129 --> 09:25.859
That's not fair! You made me say it!

09:25.965 --> 09:28.490
All right. The same thing.

09:28.601 --> 09:29.602
What do you mean?

09:29.602 --> 09:32.002
What do you mean?
The same wish as yours!

09:38.544 --> 09:41.012
Hey, where should we go next?

09:42.014 --> 09:43.242
Let's go home.

09:43.349 --> 09:46.182
Start with rock...
Rock, paper, scissors!

09:46.519 --> 09:48.680
Chocolate.

09:49.522 --> 09:51.547
Hey! Rock, paper, scissors!

09:51.657 --> 09:54.524
Pineapple.

09:55.094 --> 09:56.220
Tomari!

10:02.068 --> 10:04.901
I have one last request.

10:08.474 --> 10:10.738
Yes, I'll be fine.

10:10.843 --> 10:12.674
I'm going now.

10:38.237 --> 10:40.569
That's Hazumu's bike.

10:50.383 --> 10:53.716
It's been a while
since I rode like this.

10:53.853 --> 10:54.820
Really?

10:55.254 --> 10:59.315
You used to take me
to lots of places like this.

10:59.892 --> 11:03.521
That's because you couldn't
ride a bike for a long time.

11:03.629 --> 11:06.496
But riding like this is much easier.

11:06.599 --> 11:10.160
Usually guys are
the ones who pedal the bike.

11:10.436 --> 11:12.700
But I'm a girl now!

11:12.838 --> 11:14.237
You know...

11:14.373 --> 11:16.238
Faster, Tomari!

11:16.442 --> 11:18.706
Okay, hang on tight!

11:19.045 --> 11:21.104
Here we go!

11:21.247 --> 11:23.306
Amazing! It's so fast!

11:23.449 --> 11:24.882
Yahoo!

11:25.584 --> 11:27.814
Shall we head to the beach?

11:27.920 --> 11:29.182
The beach?

11:32.391 --> 11:35.656
Yeah, it'd be nice
if we actually could.

11:37.096 --> 11:39.326
It's too far, right?

11:45.571 --> 11:46.438
Tomari...

11:46.439 --> 11:47.531
Tomari...
Quiet.

11:48.274 --> 11:49.241
Tomari!

11:50.576 --> 11:54.512
Private Property
Feel free to walk through.

11:55.247 --> 11:58.182
Ouch, what are you doing?

11:58.584 --> 12:00.484
It's just... It's just...

12:04.690 --> 12:05.884
It's just...

12:09.729 --> 12:12.960
You have to stop
doing things like this.

12:13.466 --> 12:14.433
But...

12:15.668 --> 12:17.533
You've decided, right?

12:18.871 --> 12:19.838
Right.

12:20.539 --> 12:22.837
Then you can't cry.

12:23.209 --> 12:24.904
You're right.

12:25.244 --> 12:29.840
But you're kind to me, and I'm
being really cruel to you...

12:29.982 --> 12:32.849
You're nice and try to cheer me up.

12:33.219 --> 12:35.154
I'm sorry... I'm sorry... I'm sorry...

12:35.154 --> 12:38.021
I'm sorry... I'm sorry... I'm sorry...
Don't apologize. Don't apologize!

12:38.991 --> 12:40.822
I don't want you to.

12:43.095 --> 12:45.256
Don't worry about me...

12:45.931 --> 12:49.492
I'm happy to see you could
decide this on your own.

12:49.602 --> 12:53.003
I can be happy
with you choosing Yasuna.

12:54.273 --> 12:55.262
Tomari!

12:57.576 --> 13:02.343
You'll always be
inside my heart, Hazumu.

13:06.585 --> 13:07.711
Tomari?

13:08.420 --> 13:10.820
You crossed this river, right?

13:11.524 --> 13:14.459
You said you were
going to be my groom.

13:18.430 --> 13:23.595
<i>The Hazumu I knew back then
will always, always be mine...</i>

13:24.703 --> 13:26.398
All mine...

13:27.506 --> 13:31.909
I won't let anyone have that...
No one can take that away...

13:32.011 --> 13:33.569
That's all mine.

13:36.215 --> 13:39.514
Isn't that amazing?
That's what I have!

13:40.219 --> 13:43.848
I'll keep bragging even when
you get married and grow older.

13:43.956 --> 13:48.450
About the Hazumu who proposed
to me and confessed his love.

13:50.229 --> 13:52.197
<i>Till I get feeble and die...</i>

13:52.298 --> 13:55.893
...I'll keep bragging about it
to your kids and grandkids.

13:56.001 --> 14:01.439
I'll tell them that their mom, their
grandma, crossed a river for me.

14:02.374 --> 14:07.778
That in order to make me a bride,
you did the greatest thing in the world!

14:12.151 --> 14:15.712
Just go. You don't
need to worry about me.

14:17.356 --> 14:19.153
I'll be fine, so go.

14:19.258 --> 14:20.350
But...

14:20.726 --> 14:21.715
Go...

14:22.228 --> 14:23.217
Go!

14:26.432 --> 14:28.400
You're a man, right?

14:35.541 --> 14:36.769
Hazumu...

14:47.920 --> 14:49.751
Hazumu!

14:52.558 --> 14:53.684
No...

14:54.593 --> 14:56.720
I don't want you to go.

14:58.464 --> 14:59.453
Tomari!

15:30.029 --> 15:32.122
Yasuna is waiting for you.

15:32.231 --> 15:33.198
Yeah...

15:47.279 --> 15:52.342
Are you happy now?
Will you be my bride now?

15:52.785 --> 15:53.843
Yeah!

15:53.953 --> 15:54.885
Really?

15:55.587 --> 15:58.784
I'll be happy to be your bride!

16:25.517 --> 16:28.577
There's no way
Hazumu would come after me...

16:30.956 --> 16:34.585
Are you spying
on me? That's not cool.

16:34.893 --> 16:37.259
1 thought you might need a shoulder.

16:37.363 --> 16:39.695
I don't need your shoulder.

16:39.999 --> 16:41.023
Tomari...

16:42.134 --> 16:44.261
I have my own legs.

16:49.041 --> 16:49.939
Ayuki.

16:54.146 --> 16:56.444
I'll cry for you...

16:57.816 --> 16:59.113
Thank you...

16:59.518 --> 17:00.576
...Ayuki.

17:12.331 --> 17:15.789
Kashima Central Station

17:28.514 --> 17:29.981
I'm sorry.

17:30.349 --> 17:31.543
Thank you...

17:31.650 --> 17:32.912
Are you okay?

17:33.018 --> 17:33.985
Yes.

17:34.086 --> 17:35.644
Okay then.

17:37.322 --> 17:40.291
There are so many people here, but...

17:40.926 --> 17:43.417
I can't see anyone...

17:44.430 --> 17:46.261
I can't see...

17:47.599 --> 17:48.466
...anyone.

17:48.467 --> 17:49.661
Anyone.
Yasuna!

17:54.873 --> 17:56.238
Hazumu...

17:58.744 --> 17:59.836
Yasuna!

18:00.712 --> 18:04.011
<i>Calm down.
I want you to hear me out.</i>

18:04.817 --> 18:06.614
Hear you out?

18:07.386 --> 18:10.321
I want you to stay by my side.

18:12.191 --> 18:13.522
You're lying.

18:13.625 --> 18:15.149
I'm not lying!

18:15.394 --> 18:18.693
I decided to stay
by your side, Yasuna.

18:19.164 --> 18:20.256
So...

18:26.905 --> 18:29.237
<i>Can I believe you?</i>

18:31.677 --> 18:32.769
Hazumu!

18:33.011 --> 18:35.445
<i>Yasuna, I love you.</i>

18:46.725 --> 18:47.589
Yasuna?

18:56.502 --> 18:58.834
I can see the world...

18:59.138 --> 19:00.605
I can see!

19:02.941 --> 19:03.908
Yasuna!

19:04.076 --> 19:05.236
Hazumu!

19:06.778 --> 19:08.939
The heart that seeks someone.

19:09.047 --> 19:11.948
The heart that shows
affection for others... Love.

19:12.951 --> 19:17.285
It's difficult to talk about love.
It can't be seen with the naked eye.

19:17.389 --> 19:21.291
On the contrary,
love creates pain at times...

19:21.393 --> 19:26.126
...and you feel alienated from one
another. It even becomes a weapon.

19:26.498 --> 19:29.228
But they still seek love.

19:29.468 --> 19:31.766
That's what they live for.

19:32.638 --> 19:36.802
They feel sad when they part and
happy when they meet someone.

19:37.176 --> 19:41.943
They try to understand each other,
then laugh, cry, and get angry.

19:42.047 --> 19:44.777
And in order
to experience those things...

19:44.883 --> 19:47.249
...they seek out the love within...

19:47.719 --> 19:49.744
...and try to live.

19:51.590 --> 19:55.549
When it's time for you people
on this planet to choose...

19:55.661 --> 19:59.153
.--1 hope you don't make
the same mistakes we made.

19:59.298 --> 20:02.699
No matter how difficult
or painful it may be...

20:02.801 --> 20:07.238
...life cannot go on
without the power of love.

20:15.914 --> 20:17.472
What is this?

20:17.649 --> 20:19.014
Is it snow?

20:21.553 --> 20:23.282
No, it's light...

20:23.789 --> 20:24.790
What did you do?

20:24.790 --> 20:26.348
What did you do?
Puu...

20:26.458 --> 20:31.896
It's my parting tears for my beloved
sister brother and friends, puu...

20:32.297 --> 20:33.423
Beloved?

20:33.532 --> 20:38.560
Sister Brother is the first person
I ever kissed after all, puu.

20:39.204 --> 20:41.138
My first love.

20:41.406 --> 20:44.000
You're just a computer terminal...

20:45.310 --> 20:48.609
Love is really something.

20:48.947 --> 20:54.078
Goodbye, Sister Brother!

20:55.621 --> 20:57.088
Puu!

21:28.987 --> 21:30.614
It's pretty...

21:36.928 --> 21:37.895
Pretty...

21:38.397 --> 21:39.455
Yeah...

22:03.021 --> 22:12.396
I'll scoop up all
the tears that you shed.

22:13.598 --> 22:18.092
So please don't cry anymore.

22:18.537 --> 22:23.474
Let's walk together from now on.

22:24.976 --> 22:34.408
Even if the world
turns its back on you...

22:35.454 --> 22:48.800
...don't worry about it.
I'm always on your side.

22:49.167 --> 22:54.696
<i>What can I possibly do for you?</i>

22:55.474 --> 23:00.377
<i>That's what I was
thinking all the while.</i>

23:00.545 --> 23:10.716
1 just wanted to see you smile.

23:11.523 --> 23:14.549
I'm here for you.

23:23.335 --> 23:24.969
Thanks for waiting, Hazumu.

23:24.970 --> 23:26.130
Thanks for waiting, Hazumu.
Let's go.

23:29.307 --> 23:30.331
Hazumu?

23:40.318 --> 23:41.683
You see...

23:49.728 --> 23:50.717
Tomari!

23:52.931 --> 23:53.955
You see...
